{
  "type": "cell-height",
  "name": "cell-height",
  "description": "The three predicates of `cell-height.ts` as one probe language. Each case is a list of PROBES and the ANSWER each must give, in order. `ask: \"honorsPlan\"` is the SKIP axis (planned vs cached; `null` means absent, the string \"NaN\" means NaN — JSON carries neither); `ask: \"isDeadOnScreen\"` is the sub-pixel threshold, and also the judgement of whether a reading is a height at all — the string sentinels \"NaN\" / \"Infinity\" / \"-Infinity\" carry the values JSON has no literal for, and every one of them is DEAD (a reading that is not a height is not evidence of paint; `NaN < 1` is `false`, so the bare threshold scored it alive); `ask: \"deadColumns\"` is the REVEAL axis, one call per probe, whose `invalid` counter is orthogonal to the dead ones — it counts unusable samples in EVERY column, so one inside an otherwise-alive column is reported without that column being called dead; `ask: \"cell\"` builds one `CellHeight.of(planned, cached, measured)` triple and asks BOTH consumers about it, which is the shape that splits them (finding C2). The compile-time brand-distinctness assertions cannot be data and stay in `cell-height.deno.test.ts`.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "honorsPlan is planned-vs-cached, verbatim the === it replaced",
      "input": {
        "probes": [
          {
            "ask": "honorsPlan",
            "planned": 45,
            "cached": 45
          },
          {
            "ask": "honorsPlan",
            "planned": 45,
            "cached": 44
          },
          {
            "ask": "honorsPlan",
            "planned": 45,
            "cached": 0
          },
          {
            "ask": "honorsPlan",
            "planned": null,
            "cached": 45
          },
          {
            "ask": "honorsPlan",
            "planned": 45,
            "cached": null
          },
          {
            "ask": "honorsPlan",
            "planned": null,
            "cached": null
          },
          {
            "ask": "honorsPlan",
            "planned": "NaN",
            "cached": 45
          },
          {
            "ask": "honorsPlan",
            "planned": 45,
            "cached": "NaN"
          }
        ]
      },
      "expected": {
        "answers": [
          {
            "honorsPlan": true
          },
          {
            "honorsPlan": false
          },
          {
            "honorsPlan": false
          },
          {
            "honorsPlan": false
          },
          {
            "honorsPlan": false
          },
          {
            "honorsPlan": false
